{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f2102811-544b-4456-9e4c-d0e02c001998",
    "name": "testing",
    "description": "## Overview\n\nThis collection covers end-to-end testing of a locally hosted API (`http://localhost`) built around two core modules: **UPM (User & Project Management)** and **Analysis**.\n\n## Modules\n\n### UPM — User & Project Management\nHandles authentication and resource management for projects and tasks:\n- **Authentication** — User login (`/api/upm/login/`)\n- **Projects** — List, create, retrieve, and update projects (`/api/upm/projects/`)\n- **Tasks** — Manage and query tasks associated with projects (`/api/upm/tasks/`)\n\n### Analysis\nProvides static analysis and conflict-detection workflows:\n- **Upload Folder** — Submit a folder of source files for analysis (`/api/analysis/upload-folder/`)\n- **Detect Conflict** — Identify conflicts within uploaded content (`/api/analysis/detect-conflict/`)\n- **Test Jobs** — Create and monitor async analysis jobs (`/api/analysis/tests/jobs/`)\n- **Analysis Results** — Retrieve the output of completed analysis runs (`/api/analysis/analysis-results/`)\n\n## Usage\n\nRequests target a local development server. Ensure the backend service is running before executing any requests. Authentication should be performed first to obtain any required session tokens or credentials used by subsequent calls.\n\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "45894850",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/45894850-f2102811-544b-4456-9e4c-d0e02c001998?source=collection_link"
